<title>USA: N.Y. Pataki says objects to raising lawmakers' pay.</title>
<headline>N.Y. Pataki says objects to raising lawmakers' pay.</headline>
<dateline>ALBANY, N.Y. 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>New York State Gov. George Pataki on Tuesday reiterated he objected to raising the salaries of state lawmakers and top officials, a prospect the special session he called was rumored to be considering.</p>
<p>&quot;It's awfully late in the night for it to come up, and I've said all along my view on that, that I don't think this is the right time,&quot; he told reporters in Albany.</p>
<p>Asked about a plan to pay stipends for several leadership positions in the Senate and the Assembly, Pataki said no agreement had been reached. &quot;We're still talking about a number of issues at this point.&quot;</p>
<p>--Joan Gralla, 212-859-1654</p>
